  "summary": "New work tests design and search claims against MD dynamics, query-specific p-values and proteome-wide recoding of E. coli proteins.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is making computational protein sequence and structure judgments checkable against stricter criteria. BILBY-PRO and BILBY-MD show that static refolding success in motif scaffolding overstates dynamical fidelity when assessed by all-atom MD on 220 PROSITE-derived motifs. Struct-Caliper adds query-specific p-values to protein structure search through representation-aware randomization, improving homolog recovery and false-discovery control. The glutamine study uses ProteinMPNN and MSA conservation to rank glutamine as the most replaceable residue, then recodes 4,148 E. coli proteins. What is new is the move from point-estimate success metrics to dynamics-aware, statistically calibrated or proteome-scale validation. The previous synthesis's enzyme and VAE items are not supported by the current items.",
